---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout>
  <!-- Breadcrumbs -->
  <nav class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-8 text-sm font-medium">
    <a class="text-slate-500 hover:text-cyan-400" href="index.html">Home</a>
    <span class="text-slate-400">/</span>
    <a class="text-slate-500 hover:text-cyan-400" href="blog.html">Blog</a>
    <span class="text-slate-400">/</span>
    <span class="text-cyan-400">Bento Grid Systems</span>
  </nav>
  <!-- Bento Hero Section -->
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4 mb-12">
    <!-- Main Title Tile -->
    <div
      class="md:col-span-3 p-8 rounded-xl bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-900 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 flex flex-col justify-end min-h-[300px] relative overflow-hidden group"
    >
      <div
        class="absolute top-0 right-0 p-8 opacity-10 group-hover:opacity-20 transition-opacity"
      >
        <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-9xl text-cyan-400"
          >grid_view</span
        >
      </div>
      <div class="relative z-10">
        <div class="flex gap-2 mb-4">
          <span
            class="px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-cyan-400/10 text-cyan-400 text-xs font-bold tracking-wider uppercase"
            >Design Systems</span
          >
          <span
            class="px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-slate-200 dark:bg-slate-800 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-xs font-bold tracking-wider uppercase"
            >React</span
          >
        </div>
        <h1
          class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-black text-slate-900 dark:text-white leading-tight font-display mb-4"
        >
          Building a Bento Grid System with
          <span class="text-cyan-400">React &amp; Tailwind</span>
        </h1>
      </div>
    </div>
    <!-- Side Tiles -->
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
      <div
        class="flex-1 p-6 rounded-xl bg-cyan-400 text-neutral-950 flex flex-col justify-center items-center text-center"
      >
        <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-3xl mb-2">schedule</span>
        <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest opacity-80">
          Reading Time
        </p>
        <p class="text-2xl font-black">12 min</p>
      </div>
      <div
        class="flex-1 p-6 rounded-xl bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-900 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 flex flex-col justify-center items-center text-center"
      >
        <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-3xl mb-2 text-cyan-400"
          >calendar_today</span
        >
        <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-slate-500">
          Published
        </p>
        <p class="text-xl font-bold dark:text-white">Oct 24, 2023</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="flex flex-col lg:flex-row gap-12 relative">
    <!-- Sticky Table of Contents -->
    <aside class="hidden lg:block w-64 shrink-0 h-fit sticky top-24">
      <div
        class="p-6 rounded-xl bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-900 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800"
      >
        <h3
          class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-cyan-400 mb-6"
        >
          In this article
        </h3>
        <ul class="space-y-4">
          <li>
            <a
              class="text-sm text-cyan-400 font-bold border-l-2 border-cyan-400 pl-4 block"
              href="#intro">Introduction</a
            >
          </li>
          <li>
            <a
              class="text-sm text-slate-500 hover:text-slate-900 dark:hover:text-white border-l-2 border-transparent pl-4 block transition-colors"
              href="#philosophy">Grid Philosophy</a
            >
          </li>
          <li>
            <a
              class="text-sm text-slate-500 hover:text-slate-900 dark:hover:text-white border-l-2 border-transparent pl-4 block transition-colors"
              href="#implementation">Implementation Details</a
            >
          </li>
          <li>
            <a
              class="text-sm text-slate-500 hover:text-slate-900 dark:hover:text-white border-l-2 border-transparent pl-4 block transition-colors"
              href="#accessibility">Accessibility First</a
            >
          </li>
          <li>
            <a
              class="text-sm text-slate-500 hover:text-slate-900 dark:hover:text-white border-l-2 border-transparent pl-4 block transition-colors"
              href="#conclusion">Conclusion</a
            >
          </li>
        </ul>
        <div class="mt-8 pt-6 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
            Reading progress: <span class="text-cyan-400">45%</span>
          </p>
          <div
            class="w-full h-1 bg-slate-200 dark:bg-slate-800 mt-2 rounded-full overflow-hidden"
          >
            <div class="h-full bg-cyan-400" style="width: 45%"></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </aside>
    <!-- Main Content Area -->
    <article class="flex-1 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <div class="prose prose-slate dark:prose-invert prose-lg max-w-none">
        <p
          class="text-xl leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 font-display mb-8"
        >
          The "Bento Grid" has taken the design world by storm. Popularized by
          Apple and further refined by platforms like Linear and Vercel, this
          layout pattern isn't just about looking pretty—it's about information
          density and visual hierarchy.
        </p>
        <h2
          class="text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-12 mb-6 font-display"
          id="intro"
        >
          Introduction
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-6 leading-loose text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-400">
          Modern interfaces are moving away from the standard list-view layouts.
          Users crave data-rich environments that feel structured yet organic.
          By utilizing CSS Grid and Tailwind CSS, we can create these layouts
          with surprising ease while maintaining perfect responsiveness.
        </p>
        <!-- Image with Caption -->
        <figure class="my-10">
          <div
            class="rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800"
          >
            <img
              alt="Interface Design"
              class="w-full h-auto grayscale hover:grayscale-0 transition-all duration-700"
              data-alt="Abstract dark grid of computer interfaces"
              src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/aida-public/AB6AXuBvGGUnmGlUtjzTlDhTWz6__Bq6YljyBBsSdHD7SWFIA2sFsyMz0LtR8DWCznHIr_PU814PxJ7j69htAZRL5k2tSKqbfs4wbF0NpCmay_jS5bw5-KIH2hySqISO0vzB7CXhaLYcE-7GsbOhjrevx_W6hj6bFEDarkg0Jr8kScxr-eYql5DhhVyN5bFD2Bd_sjeOGPpn18nwj1XZLimQof8d-5dUGg0vxjz_pBRrkpRgSxkw9fg0mmErc7a7kGNLWcmFA46CBuuOWAA"
            />
          </div>
          <figcaption class="text-sm text-slate-500 mt-4 text-center">
            Fig 1.1: The anatomy of a high-density bento grid component.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <!-- Key Takeaway Block -->
        <div
          class="my-10 p-8 rounded-xl bg-cyan-400/5 border-l-4 border-cyan-400"
        >
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-cyan-400 mb-2">
            <span class="material-symbols-outlined">lightbulb</span>
            <span class="font-bold text-sm uppercase tracking-wider"
              >Key Takeaway</span
            >
          </div>
          <p
            class="text-slate-900 dark:text-white text-lg italic leading-relaxed"
          >
            Bento grids work best when the content varies in importance. Use
            size to dictate where the user's eye should land first.
          </p>
        </div>
        <h2
          class="text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-12 mb-6 font-display"
          id="philosophy"
        >
          Grid Philosophy
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-6 leading-loose text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-400">
          When designing a Bento system, think in "units". Each tile should
          represent a distinct piece of information. Whether it's a code
          snippet, a metric, or an image gallery, the border radius and spacing
          must remain consistent to hold the visual metaphor together.
        </p>
        <!-- Code Block -->
        <div
          class="my-10 rounded-xl bg-[#081212] border border-slate-800 overflow-hidden"
        >
          <div
            class="flex justify-between items-center px-4 py-2 bg-slate-900 border-b border-slate-800"
          >
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-slate-400">BentoGrid.tsx</span>
            <button
              class="text-xs text-cyan-400 flex items-center gap-1 hover:underline"
            >
              <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-sm">content_copy</span
              >
              Copy
            </button>
          </div>

          <span class="code-syntax">export default</span>
          <span class="text-white">BentoItem</span>;
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
    <p class="mb-6 leading-loose text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-400">
      The use of <code>hover:scale-[1.02]</code> adds a layer of depth, making the
      tiles feel tangible. In dark mode, we specifically use subtle gradients or cyan-400
      color glows to highlight these interactions.
    </p>
  </div>
  <!-- Tags Footer -->
  <div
    class="mt-16 pt-8 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 flex flex-wrap gap-2"
  >
    <span
      class="text-slate-500 text-sm font-bold mr-2 self-center uppercase tracking-widest"
      >Tagged:</span
    >
    <div
      class="flex h-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center gap-x-2 rounded-lg bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 px-4"
    >
      <p
        class="text-slate-900 dark:text-white text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wider"
      >
        Frontend
      </p>
    </div>
    <div
      class="flex h-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center gap-x-2 rounded-lg bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 px-4"
    >
      <p
        class="text-slate-900 dark:text-white text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wider"
      >
        Tailwind
      </p>
    </div>
    <div
      class="flex h-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center gap-x-2 rounded-lg bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 px-4"
    >
      <p
        class="text-slate-900 dark:text-white text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wider"
      >
        UX Design
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<!-- Related Articles Bento Row -->
<section class="mt-24">
  <h2
    class="text-2xl font-black text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-8 font-display"
  >
    Related Reading
  </h2>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
    <!-- Related Item 1 -->
    <a
      class="group p-6 rounded-xl bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-900 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 hover:border-cyan-400 transition-all duration-300 flex flex-col gap-4"
      href="#"
    >
      <div
        class="w-full aspect-video rounded-lg bg-slate-200 dark:bg-slate-800 overflow-hidden"
      >
        <img
          alt="Article preview"
          class="w-full h-full object-cover grayscale group-hover:grayscale-0 transition-all duration-500"
          data-alt="Blue react logo on dark tech background"
          src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/aida-public/AB6AXuCa5Up-IdXaYLFStCqV5T0uw2mo2pucV_xaZY5rPakONLBn9QwjIobLfmldjTyt1-Q9J_GKe1Onc5ZTcUW9kxBIeRItobA7GcDQ5rhKQxMSDnQwKoovnn6Ly8G9PdSCos9HSdk9heVIOh_GaHRd7eYv4fu-m0dobFT-a_Zq_T1GgqIG1QU6tr-DZpT8VmWU3itaRj3pj8666YqX0u2aXHOD1lUVu5Hl1ni-otn1QyzhJPM673OlCZ-w9TIFJkaI3bp203F_4t_hWmk"
        />
      </div>
      <div>
        <p
          class="text-cyan-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest mb-2"
        >
          Development
        </p>
        <h3
          class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white group-hover:text-cyan-400 transition-colors font-display"
        >
          Optimizing React Hooks for Performance
        </h3>
      </div>
    </a>
    <!-- Related Item 2 -->
    <a
      class="group p-6 rounded-xl bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-900 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 hover:border-cyan-400 transition-all duration-300 flex flex-col gap-4"
      href="#"
    >
      <div
        class="w-full aspect-video rounded-lg bg-slate-200 dark:bg-slate-800 overflow-hidden"
      >
        <img
          alt="Article preview"
          class="w-full h-full object-cover grayscale group-hover:grayscale-0 transition-all duration-500"
          data-alt="Cyberpunk code on a monitor"
          src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/aida-public/AB6AXuB8aV1eulDrIVtoL8MsYaUTnEzOhKmKFbYG7dQmVChnur5sawwnHyhWxJ4L2imFsLnLgA46MfC6k6B0Hy1embSgnjD-gAMdcH7dgryOoJ-4W6-Tx1vzd0eV7pj0kB_oh3KlzwseRyy7hxZPb_s73EZhR8WMY3MQv0RhMzGRdxx28iK1FztCnQmcJ-yK6G6mzwZU46-5bBKczBEq9iH2-2l3o-3CwfGAV4DvjxRPg5gM5W2l4hchylvNrEiHwB_TmCMVR28AedLMl-g"
        />
      </div>
      <div>
        <p
          class="text-cyan-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest mb-2"
        >
          Workflow
        </p>
        <h3
          class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white group-hover:text-cyan-400 transition-colors font-display"
        >
          My Developer Setup for 2024
        </h3>
      </div>
    </a>
    <!-- Related Item 3 (Newsletter Bento Tile) -->
    <div
      class="p-8 rounded-xl bg-cyan-400 flex flex-col justify-between text-neutral-950"
    >
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-black mb-2 font-display">Keep in the loop</h3>
        <p class="text-sm font-medium opacity-80 leading-relaxed">
          Weekly insights on UI/UX and React internals delivered to your inbox.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-col gap-2">
        <input
          class="bg-white/20 border-white/20 placeholder:text-neutral-950/60 text-neutral-950 rounded-lg text-sm px-4 py-2 focus:ring-neutral-950"
          placeholder="your@email.com"
        />
        <button
          class="bg-neutral-950 text-white font-bold py-2 px-4 rounded-lg text-sm hover:opacity-90 transition-opacity"
        >
          Subscribe
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
